@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `usca-assessed-value`

-- Tests of usca-assessed-value.l4 (Gov. Code § 25).  Each expected value is decided from the section cited above the assertion, before the run.
-- A fiscal year is given by the first calendar year in its name: 1980 is the 1980-81 fiscal year.  A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Gov. Code § 25(a): 25 percent of full value to and including 1980-81, 100 percent from 1981-82`

#ASSERT `the percent of full value that assessed value is in the fiscal year` 1980 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `the percent of full value that assessed value is in the fiscal year` 1979 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `the percent of full value that assessed value is in the fiscal year` 1900 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `the percent of full value that assessed value is in the fiscal year` 1981 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the percent of full value that assessed value is in the fiscal year` 2026 EQUALS 100

#ASSERT `the assessed value of property whose full value is` 1000000 `in the fiscal year` 1980 EQUALS 250000
#ASSERT `the assessed value of property whose full value is` 1000000 `in the fiscal year` 1981 EQUALS 1000000
#ASSERT `the assessed value of property whose full value is` 400000 `in the fiscal year` 1975 EQUALS 100000

-- Tax rates are expressed in dollars on each $100 of assessed value to and including 1980-81, and as a percentage of full value from 1981-82.
#ASSERT `the way tax rates are expressed in the fiscal year` 1980 EQUALS `dollars, or fractions thereof, on each one hundred dollars ($100) of assessed value`
#ASSERT `the way tax rates are expressed in the fiscal year` 1981 EQUALS `a percentage of full value`
#ASSERT `the way tax rates are expressed in the fiscal year` 2026 EQUALS `a percentage of full value`

§ `Gov. Code § 25(b): comparisons for different years are made on the same basis`

-- An assessed value of 250,000 in a 25 percent year stands for 1,000,000 of full value, so it is 1,000,000 in a 100 percent year, and back.
#ASSERT `an amount of assessed value restated for comparison` 250000 1980 1981 EQUALS 1000000
#ASSERT `an amount of assessed value restated for comparison` 1000000 1981 1980 EQUALS 250000
-- An exemption stated as 7,000 of assessed value in a 25 percent year has the same relative value as 28,000 in a 100 percent year.
#ASSERT `an amount of assessed value restated for comparison` 7000 1980 1981 EQUALS 28000
-- Two years on the same basis need no adjustment.
#ASSERT `an amount of assessed value restated for comparison` 250000 1979 1980 EQUALS 250000
#ASSERT `an amount of assessed value restated for comparison` 1000000 1990 2000 EQUALS 1000000

-- A rate of $4 on each $100 of assessed value (a 25 percent year) is 1 percent of full value, written as the fraction 0.01 (fork F-25c); and back.
#ASSERT `a tax rate restated for comparison` 4 1980 1981 EQUALS 0.01
#ASSERT `a tax rate restated for comparison` 0.01 1981 1980 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `a tax rate restated for comparison` 4 1979 1980 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `a tax rate restated for comparison` 0.01 1990 2000 EQUALS 0.01

-- "the same amount of tax revenues would be produced": the tax on a property is the rate on each $100 of assessed value times its assessed value, or the fraction of its full value.
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
      `the full value of the property` IS A NUMBER
      `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax the rate produces` rate `the full value of the property` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` MEANS
    IF `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` LESS THAN 1981
    THEN rate TIMES (`the full value of the property` TIMES 25 DIVIDED BY 100) DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE rate TIMES `the full value of the property`

#ASSERT `the tax the rate produces` 4 1000000 1980 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the tax the rate produces` 0.01 1000000 1981 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the tax the rate produces` (`a tax rate restated for comparison` 4 1980 1981) 1000000 1981 EQUALS `the tax the rate produces` 4 1000000 1980
#ASSERT `the tax the rate produces` (`a tax rate restated for comparison` 3.5 1979 1981) 123456 1981 EQUALS `the tax the rate produces` 3.5 123456 1979
#ASSERT `the tax the rate produces` (`a tax rate restated for comparison` 0.0125 1990 1980) 654321 1980 EQUALS `the tax the rate produces` 0.0125 654321 1990

§ `Gov. Code § 25(c): the conversion factors, twenty-five hundredths of 1 percent and 400`

#ASSERT `a rate in dollars on each $100 of assessed value at a 25 percent assessment ratio, restated as comparable to a percentage of full value` 4 EQUALS 0.01
#ASSERT `a rate expressed as a percentage of full value, restated as comparable to dollars on each $100 of assessed value at a 25 percent assessment ratio` 0.01 EQUALS 4
-- The two factors undo each other (fork F-25c): 0.0025 times 400 is 1.
#ASSERT `a rate expressed as a percentage of full value, restated as comparable to dollars on each $100 of assessed value at a 25 percent assessment ratio` (`a rate in dollars on each $100 of assessed value at a 25 percent assessment ratio, restated as comparable to a percentage of full value` 3.5) EQUALS 3.5
-- Subdivision (c) agrees with the restatement subdivision (b) asks for.
#ASSERT `a rate in dollars on each $100 of assessed value at a 25 percent assessment ratio, restated as comparable to a percentage of full value` 2.75 EQUALS `a tax rate restated for comparison` 2.75 1980 1981
#ASSERT `a rate expressed as a percentage of full value, restated as comparable to dollars on each $100 of assessed value at a 25 percent assessment ratio` 0.0125 EQUALS `a tax rate restated for comparison` 0.0125 1981 1980

-- assertions written: 30
